  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On rue du Lys, opposite the square des Frères Gaudino Joly, the city of Cannes opened this 400 m² dog park on 23 December 2024. It is fully fenced (a fence 145 metres long and 1.20 m high) with two entrances, and has a meadow, a stabilised area to collect waste, an agility course (walkway and seesaw), a fountain for dogs and their owners, a hose to clean them, two waste-bag dispensers, two bins, three benches and nine ornamental trees. According to the City, no parking space was removed to create it.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The park is open every day from 8:30am to 6:30pm (source: city of Cannes). Dogs must stay under their owner's supervision and have up-to-date vaccinations, and category 1 and 2 dogs are not allowed. Remember to pick up waste.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: remember bags (two dispensers on site) and the fountain, but there is no access for category 1 and 2 dogs.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The park is located in front of the square des frères Gaudino Joly, in the heart of the town centre. According to the municipal magazine Cannes Soleil (November 2026), other places are open to dogs by municipal decision, such as the square Colonel Arnaud Beltrame, as well as the Midi, Zamenhof, Gazagnaire and Brigitte Bardot beaches from 1 November to 1 May; the City's "Animal citadin" page lists the Midi, Zamenhof and Gazagnaire beaches without time restrictions during this period (see the Cannes beach pages). The magazine also mentions the Croix-des-Gardes and the lower Siagne valley as large walking areas.</p>
    </div>

